{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":59.97999954223633,"text":"It all began with a hole in a vineyard. In January 1506, a farmer digging on the Escaline Hill found a marble group—a man and his two sons wrestling with sea serpents. Pope Julius II sent Michelangelo to look at it, bought it, and put it in a courtyard of his palace for everyone to admire. That courtyard was the first room of the Vatican Museums. Five hundred years later, the museums hold about 70,000 works—20,000 of them on display—in 24 collections—Egyptian mummies, Greek and Roman statues, a 120-meter corridor of painted maps, Raphael's rooms, and, at the very end, the Sistine Chapel, with the ceiling Michelangelo painted standing on scaffolding. In 2024, 6.8 million visitors came through—more than any museum in the world except the Louvre—and you leave down a double-spiral staircase, where the people going up never meet the people coming down.","words":[{"word":"It","start":0,"end":0.3799999952316284},{"word":"all","start":0.3799999952316284,"end":0.7400000095367432},{"word":"began","start":0.7400000095367432,"end":0.9200000166893005},{"word":"with","start":0.9200000166893005,"end":1.2400000095367432},{"word":"a","start":1.2400000095367432,"end":1.5800000429153442},{"word":"hole","start":1.5800000429153442,"end":1.7000000476837158},{"word":"in","start":1.7000000476837158,"end":1.9199999570846558},{"word":"a","start":1.9199999570846558,"end":2.380000114440918},{"word":"vineyard","start":2.380000114440918,"end":2.4000000953674316},{"word":"In","start":3.0399999618530273,"end":3.0799999237060547},{"word":"January","start":3.0799999237060547,"end":3.619999885559082},{"word":"1506","start":3.619999885559082,"end":4.699999809265137},{"word":"a","start":5.059999942779541,"end":5.559999942779541},{"word":"farmer","start":5.559999942779541,"end":5.559999942779541},{"word":"digging","start":5.559999942779541,"end":5.900000095367432},{"word":"on","start":5.900000095367432,"end":6.119999885559082